# Path to the SQLite database file (inside the /data volume when running in Docker)
PULSE_DB=/data/pulse.sqlite

# On first run, navigate to http://localhost:3002 and create your admin account.
# No manual DB setup required.

# ── Public exposure (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# When you expose the consumer PWA publicly (e.g. behind a Cloudflare tunnel),
# pin the public hostname so ONLY /app is served there and the whole admin
# cockpit returns 404 (admin stays LAN-only):
# PULSE_PUBLIC_HOST=pulse.example.com
#
# If you sit behind a reverse proxy / tunnel, read the real client IP from the
# forwarded header so per-IP rate-limiting works per visitor (not per-proxy):
# ADDRESS_HEADER=X-Forwarded-For
# XFF_DEPTH=1
#
# Public-facing URLs for the viewer's "Watch / Request / See more" links and
# per-item deep-links. Internal data + posters are still fetched over each
# connection's baseUrl — these only change links the viewer clicks. Leave unset
# for LAN-only use (falls back to baseUrl).
# PULSE_PUBLIC_JELLYFIN_URL=https://watch.example.com
# PULSE_PUBLIC_SEERR_URL=https://request.example.com
# PULSE_PUBLIC_PLEX_URL=https://plex.example.com

# ── Trakt.tv sync (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Lets each consumer link their own Trakt account so finished plays are pushed
# to their Trakt history. Without BOTH values the feature is completely inert:
# no linking, no syncing — pulse simply skips it.
#
# Register an application at https://trakt.tv/oauth/applications and set its
# redirect URI to urn:ietf:wg:oauth:2.0:oob (pulse uses the device-code flow,
# so no callback URL is needed).
# PULSE_TRAKT_CLIENT_ID=
# PULSE_TRAKT_CLIENT_SECRET=
